  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The findings are based on trip data from a single city, Melbourne, which may limit generalizability to cities with different transit layouts or pricing structures.",
      "what": "This study calculated and compared the total generalised cost of shared e-scooter trips in Melbourne against their equivalent public transport alternatives. The analysis identifies specific spatial and temporal conditions where e-scooters outperform transit, particularly for non-radial journeys, trips near entertainment venues, and travel during late evening hours.",
      "why": "It maps the precise service gaps of public transport networks by demonstrating where and when micro-mobility options offer a more cost- and time-effective alternative for urban travelers."
    }
